From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:54:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] search: a thread caches a tag it finds, not only one it makes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Search::findTag looks a tag up in the visiting thread's tag cache
first and in the shared tag_set_ under tag_lock_ only on a miss, but
only a tag the thread made itself went into its cache. A tag another
thread made was looked up under tag_lock_ every time this thread met
it again. On a 64 x 256 register file's write_timing_model at 48
threads (OpenROAD#11999), futex syscalls and the kernel's queued spin
lock were over half of the samples, with Search::findTag and
Search::mutateTag the first STA frames above them.

A tag found in tag_set_ now goes into the thread's cache too. The
cache is the visitor copy's, which lives for one parallel visit, and
tags are deleted only on the main thread between visits.

A cache hit also deleted nothing when findTag owned the states it was
given; it deletes them now, as the tag_set_ hit below it does.

Not upstreamed. Carried in bazel-orfs; retires on the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD whose OpenSTA carries it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 search/Search.cc | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sta/search/Search.cc b/src/sta/search/Search.cc
index bda5ab24..8d06a89b 100644
--- a/src/sta/search/Search.cc
+++ b/src/sta/search/Search.cc
@@ -3029,12 +3029,19 @@ Search::findTag(Scene *scene,
             states, false);
   if (tag_cache) {
     Tag *tag = findKey(*tag_cache, &probe);
-    if (tag)
+    if (tag) {
+      if (own_states)
+        delete states;
       return tag;
+    }
   }
 
   LockGuard lock(tag_lock_);
   Tag *tag = findKey(*tag_set_, &probe);
+  if (tag && tag_cache)
+    // Another thread made it: cache it here too, or every lookup of it
+    // from this thread takes tag_lock_.
+    tag_cache->insert(tag);
   if (tag == nullptr) {
     // Make rise/fall versions of the tag to avoid tag_set lookups when the
     // only change is the rise/fall edge.
